# TypeScript Standards

- Strict mode on. No `any` — use `unknown` + narrowing, or a precise type.
- Validate all external input (API bodies, queue payloads) with a schema (e.g. Zod) at the boundary.
- Prefer named exports; one responsibility per module.
- Shared domain types live in `packages/core`; DB types come from Prisma — don't redefine them.

## Error handling

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
try { await extract(event); } catch (e) {}

// ✅ GOOD
try {
  await extract(event);
} catch (e) {
  logger.error("extraction failed", { eventId: event.id, error: e });
  throw new ExtractionError("Failed to extract facts", { cause: e });
}
```

- Throw typed errors that map to API status codes (`401/402/429/404/422`).
- Never swallow errors silently in workers — let BullMQ retry or fail the job explicitly.
